4. Add/remove live sources to compose preview (WO-323)  [decision: drag any Live-tab source onto
   the freeform tiles surface, multiviewer-style]
   ⛔ IMPLEMENTED then REVERTED (2026-07-22, on-box test failed). First cut reused the operator-gui
      'mvcell' + srcCh model (whole-channel routing). BUG found live: a DeckLink input is NOT a whole
      channel — its route is channel-LAYER, e.g. `route://6-4` (ch 6, layer 4; channelMap
      inputChannels[].route). The mvcell/srcCh model can only represent `route://<ch>`, so it drops the
      layer → wrong/blank content (owner: "none of the windows display any content" after adding
      DeckLink). Reverted operator-compose-tiles.js + CSS + wo256 test + rebuilt dist-web → working
      compose restored (reload kiosk).
      V2 IMPLEMENTED 2026-07-22 (full route string, like the working multiview). SERVER (additive):
      operator-gui-channel computeOperatorGuiCellPlan + resolveCellSourceChannel now PLAY a cell's
      explicit `route` string verbatim (route://6-4), extracting the channel only for the WO-156/dims
      guards; pgm/prv + whole-channel cells unchanged. operator-gui-mode layout body carries `route`.
      CLIENT: operator-compose-tiles drop keeps the full route value (parseSourceDropPayload →
      {route, srcCh, label}), source-tile own store, srcCh-keyed seed, remove ✕. Tests: wo243 route
