5. Operator GUI on the multiview port / headless / remote stream (WO-324 superseded by WO-325)
   ✅ Operator GUI can now be HEADLESS (`headless:true` on the destination) — no `<screen>` consumer,
      no kiosk, no stolen multiview port; the gui-stream (channel 5) is unaffected. Set on this box's
      Operator GUI destination; verified the regenerated Caspar config drops its `<screen>` (3→2
      screen consumers). Needs a node restart + Caspar config regenerate/restart to take on the box.
   ✅ Remote stream "doesn't work" = access, not a bug: the laptop must use https://<box-ip>:4443
      (WebCodecs needs a secure context; plain http://:4200 can't decode). Added a secure-context
      HINT in Settings → Compose preview when Live stream is picked on an insecure origin (WO-325B).

15. Save 409 "payload older than stored" (line 15)
   🔎 Diagnosed, NOT a code bug: box is on Etc/UTC and `System clock synchronized: no`; the client is
      ~2h off in ABSOLUTE (UTC) time even though the wall-clock faces match. savedAt is UTC, so the
      client's saves look "older". Fix: NTP + correct timezone on BOTH. Durable code fix (server-
      issued monotonic `rev` instead of a client wall-clock) proposed but not implemented (would touch
      load-bearing save/anti-resurrect logic).

17. "can't uncheck autostart gui" (line 17)
   ✅ Fixed. The device-view updateDestination merge (src/api/device-view-crud.js) only carried
      explicitly-listed patch fields for operator_gui (guiUrl/physicalPort) and let `…d0` keep the
      rest — so a patched `autoLaunch:false` was dropped and the box always re-checked. Now autoLaunch
      (and headless) are honoured on patch. Server-only — needs a node restart. Regression test added
      to smoke-wo243-operator-gui.test.js. (The Devices inspector already has the "Auto-start at boot"
      checkbox; it just wasn't sticking.)
 
